    "media:imagetext": "#3\nOct. 28th.\nThis morning Harry Smith, the pilot who supplied\nthe pheasants, had another treat for us.\nSmith used to fly for\nchiang-Kai-shek.\nYesterday he bumped into an. acquaintance attached\nto the Generalissimo's entourage.\nThe party in question had Just\nreturned from Hami, \u0026 city in far western Sinkiang Province where\nhe had secured for\nthe Generalissimo - either as an incident to,\nor the objective of, his excursion, some Hami melons.\nhe gave unbeknownst to c.K.s.) to\nHarry Smith.\nIn the old days the\nchinese emperors used to operate a pony express from Hami to Peking\nduring the melon season.\nThe horsemen, descendants of Genghis Khan's\ncavalrymen, rode night and day to rush\nthe melons to the Capital.\ncan well understand.\nThe melon 1s like a honey dew, only much better.\nThey are the size of small watermelon.\nThe mean is firm and crisp.\nThey are perfectly delicious, but apparently cannot be raised anywhere\nelse in the world except around Hami.\nWe had a busy time today. A morning long session with our CNAC\npartners going over the business of the last two months since the\nthe afternoon we journeyed across the Yangssze to Wuchang to visit\nthe airplane factory which was moved here after the Japs attacked it\nat Hangchow.\nIt was very interesting as\nwe were shown around by one\nof our old men, Wong Su;\nand he told us all about the bombing of\nHangehow - a hectic move by truck, train, river and coolle power.\nTonight we dine at 8 with the American Consul, Mr.Josselyn.\nam going to mail this letter now by Eurasia to Hongkong and from there\nby Clipper to my secretary Miss Forbes, who is staying with the family\nat Baguio. She will make a number of\ntypewritten copies and mail from\nthe Phillippines.\nAnother installment will follow some time soon.\nWe are leaving tomorrow, Oct.28th, for Nanking, by British steamer.\nThere it will not be so quiet and peaceful as here but I think quite\nsafe. Conditions on the spot are never as bad as the newspapers would\nlead you to believe. The further removed from the scene the worse\nthe reports.\nAs ever,\nн. м.В.\nfabulo, Nov. 2nd\nDear Will, Ruth, Donald \u0026 Ralph:\nWe haven't heard anything further from Harold, but trust the next\nHe did remember\nManila Bay.\nwas very good and our first since han leaving China.\nyours are keeping well.\nHope you and\nAs ever,\nDebby\n-3-",
